Netflix has released a trailer for Ava DuVernay 's compelling and urgent documentary 14 th , ahead of its November 27 theatrical release and December 4 debut on the streaming platform. Watch it above.

The Oscar-contending film argues the 14 th Amendment of the Constitution, passed in the wake of the Civil War, laid the groundwork for America's multiracial democracy. It explores how the MAGA movement has made it a priority to dismantle the rights enumerated in that amendment.

"We are all at peril," law professor Sherrilyn Ifill comments in the trailer. "If we don't think it's coming for us, we are so sadly mistaken." Former Georgia State Representative Stacey Abrams notes, "The whole of the 14 th is under assault. If the 14 th falls, then every other right that it guarantees is now in jeopardy." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

One of the amendment's five provisions mandates birthright citizenship &#x2013; meaning anyone born in the United States is considered a citizen. The Trump administration has attempted to circumvent that as part of its broader attack on immigration. In the trailer, Vice President JD Vance says, "The concept of birthright citizenship is an absurdity." Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

In June, the U.S. Supreme Court struck down the president's executive order that declared children born in the U.S. to parents in the country unlawfully were not entitled to birthright citizenship. But the decision was by no means unanimous. Conservative Justices Clarence Thomas, Samuel Alito, and Neil Gorsuch dissented.

14 th premiered at the New York Film Festival in October and screened this weekend at IDFA in Amsterdam, the world's biggest documentary festival. We spoke with DuVernay briefly before her IDFA Q&A Sunday night and she told us she hopes people will take seriously threats to the 14 th Amendment and not be lulled into complacency by the results of the midterm elections, which delivered a decisive repudiation of the president and his policies.

14 th is produced by DuVernay, Spencer Averick, Paul Garnes, and Tammy Thomas-Garnes. Samantha Casey serves as archival producer. Spencer Averick edited the film; the cinematography is by Cliff Charles and Michael Fernandez. The score is composed by Jason Moran. The film is a production of Array Filmworks. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

DuVernay earned an Academy Award nomination for her previous documentary, 13 th . In October, she won the Documentary Filmmaker Award at the Montclair Film Festival in New Jersey and 14 th won the Audience Award for Documentary Feature at the Middleburg Film Festival in Virginia.

Watch the trailer for 14 th above.

Jalen Rose, the NBA star-turned media personality, is launching his own talk and variety show, Pop The Trunk , he tells The Hollywood Reporter. The show will debut in January, with twice-weekly episodes running on YouTube and other podcast platforms.

Rose played for six teams in his career (his longest tenure was with the Indiana Pacers) before moving into broadcasting, where he worked for Fox Sports , NBC Sports and TNT Sports, though it is his run as a basketball analyst at ESPN where he is likely best known to sports fans. Related Stories TV The 2026 NWSL Semifinal: Where to Watch Gotham FC vs. Kansas City Current TV Where to Watch Texas vs. LSU Football Game Online

In fact, it was his work on Fox's Best Damn Sports Show and on his Jalen & Jacoby podcast for ESPN that inspired Pop The Trunk . blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#8220;I was really fortunate to get into the multimedia space while I was still a player in the NBA, working on the Best Damn Sports Show ,&#8221; he tells THR , adding that his segments there inspired him to pitch Bill Simmons (then the head of ESPN's Grantland) on what became Jalen & Jacoby . &#8220;I was always proud of the content of the show. We used sports as a backdrop, you know. If Benny the Butcher is at a Bills game, he's the correspondent. We were running a different race with story times and animations and things of that nature, these are all things things that I still don't see happening in the marketplace that I'm excited to bring back as a brainchild.&#8221;

Rose compares Pop The Trunk to an old-school TV variety show, with interviews, live performances, skits, animated segments and more, adding that he is &#8220;going to draw inspiration from the shows of the golden era, like when it was appointment viewing.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#8220;I grew up watching Saturday Night Live and In Living Color , Dave Chappelle, and when you turn on those shows, you don't know who's gonna be on the show. So that's kind of what I'm looking to recreate,&#8221; Rose adds. &#8220;I've done the sitting in front of the microphone show for an hour, I've done that on television, I've done that on radio, and I've done it in podcasts. And so this is a graduation of that idea.&#8221;

So what can viewers expect? Rose says the A block will likely be a monologue (&#8220;it's probably going to upset a lot of people, but similar to like what you might consider a roast of whatever current event topics are happening,&#8221; he quips) though the next segments will evolve over time.

&#8220;Then the guest on the show, for example, whoever it is, will get a chance to hear what I say and agree or disagree with what I have to say, and then we'll get into the hot button topics that are happening around fashion, sports, entertainment, multimedia, life, politics, whatever, and have people that are knowledgeable about those topics on to discuss them and create quality content. It's not gonna just be me sitting in front of a black microphone for an hour and a half.&#8221;

Sada Baby and Detroit Diamond are among the confirmed recurring guests.

But Pop The Trunk is also serving as a launchpad of sorts for Same Page Entertainment, the Detroit-based media and production company founded by Rose and Platinum Equity founder, chairman and CEO, and Detroit Pistons owner Tom Gores. The company has, so far, released South West High for Tubi, and has wrapped production on the film The Streak , which stars Ed Helms. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

During the conversation with THR , Rose took a call from someone working on the set in downtown Detroit, underscoring the work that he and Gores are doing.

&#8220;The person that just called me was actually calling me about the LED screen that they're putting in the studio, so along with my partner Tom Gores and Same Page Entertainment and our team, I'm building a company plus launching a show, so it's brick by brick,&#8221; Rose says. &#8220;The theme song, which really doesn't exist for shows right now, it's the animations, the story times. Those are things that fans loved from me back in the day that we were able to do and create a level of enthusiasm for us.&#8221;

Netflix has released the trailer for the political documentary " 14th ," analyzing the history of the U.S. Constitution's amendment and the risks of its weakening power.

Directed by Ava DuVernay , the film follows her "13th" documentary, which examined racial injustices within the American prison system. "Written in the wreckage of the Civil War, the 14th Amendment was meant to close the door on the hierarchy of human worth,&#8221; reads the logline. &#8220;Instead, it has become a permanent argument." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Taylor Swift’s Canceled Vienna Concerts Due to Thwarted Terrorist Plot to Be Subject of Documentary Olivia Rodrigo's 'Take Me Home (4 Christmas)' Effusively Endorsed by Writer of the Waitresses' 'Christmas Wrapping,' Who Praises Her for Picking Up the 'Vibe' 45 Years Later

The main tenet of the 14th Amendment grants citizenship to all persons born or naturalized in the United States. The documentary explores the potential consequences of removing or diminishing this right. Congresswomen Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez and Anna Paulina Luna, former Senator Jeff Flake and current Senator Alex Padilla, plus legal minds Sherrilyn Ifill, Robert Chang and Stacey Abrams are among the historians, lawyers, scholars, curators and politicians lending their voice to the documentary as DuVernay chronicles the vicious battle over the amendment that has raged for over 150 years. "14th" brings together voices in direct conversation with a question America still hasn't settled: Who gets to belong?

Speaking with Variety before the election which saw Democrats win control of both the House and Senate, DuVernay said , &#8220;Folks need to really understand what it means to be a citizen, what it means to fight and to really know your rights.&#8221;

Variety's senior film critic Owen Gleiberman wrote that the documentary &#8220;exerts the same kind of historical/topical force that &#x2018;13th' did. DuVernay, while she works in an extremely accessible and mainstream way, has a singular gift for making the nuances of history come alive." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The documentary releases in select theaters on Nov. 27 before releasing globally on Netflix on Dec. 4. DuVernay also serves as a producer along with Spencer Averick, Tammy Garnes and Paul Garnes. Spencer Averick is the editor, and Michael Cambio Fernandez and Clifford Charles are the directors of photography. The score is composed by Jason Moran.

Russell Brand &#8216;s message from prison on Sunday &#x2014; in which he asserted his innocence after being convicted of rape and sexual assault &#x2014; is being investigated by the U.K. Ministry of Justice.

The Guardian reported on Monday that the message Brand's wife , Laura Gallacher, read out on their &#8220;Sunday Service&#8221; podcast could have broken prison rules. &#8220;Beloved brothers and sisters in Christ, God bless you for your support,&#8221; Brand wrote in a statement read by Gallacher. &#8220;As you know, I am not guilty for the offenses I have been jailed for, so something strange is happening." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Beyoncé Makes Grammys History as First Artist With 100 Nominations Grammy Nominations 2027: The Complete List (Updating Live)

A spokesperson for U.K. Prime Minister Andy Burnham told The Guardian: &#8220;This is clearly appalling and is being urgently investigated. We expect action to be taken if he's found to have broken the rules. Prisoners are strictly banned from making statements that cause distress to victims and speaking to the media is only permitted in exceptional circumstances. Prisoners cannot get around these rules by having someone else publish their comments.&#8221;

Victims' Commissioner for London Andrea Simon told BBC News that Brand's message will &#8220;certainly retraumatize his victims and other survivors of rape who have to hear it.&#8221;

In a statement to Sky News, U.K. foreign secretary Ed Miliband called Brand's crimes &#8220;heinous and awful,&#8221; adding that &#8220;it's revolting that he shows no remorse today in his comments.&#8221;

Brand has just started a prison sentence of 10 years and six months after being convicted of three counts of sexual assault and one count of rape in a highly publicized criminal trial in London. The former actor and comedian was found not guilty of two other rape charges and a count of attempted indecent assault.

EXCLUSIVE: Nearly three years after they first sat down , British actors union Equity is finally taking a deal to its members from producer trade body Pact .

The new deal for actors on the majority of British shows and movies, starting January 1 2027 through December 31 2029, includes everything from pay to streamer compensation to self-tapes, but it is artificial intelligence that has delayed things time and time again.

After years of on-off negotiations and several strike threats, we can reveal that Equity is now taking a final offer to its 8,000-strong actor member base with a recommendation to vote &#8220;yes.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); } Related Stories News SAG-AFTRA Boss Says AI Takedowns Matter More Than Damages To Performers News Will The Congressional Blue Tsunami Help Or Hurt The Plan To Save Hollywood?

That offer features a &#8220;groundbreaking agreement on protections for artists over their digital likeness alongside vital safeguards that prioritize human creativity in the industry,&#8221; Equity said.

After much tussling, Equity said the AI element of the Pact offer is &#8220;significantly improved&#8221; and is four-pronged, with protections for the creation and use of digital replicas, protections relating to digital alterations of your performance, protections against "Synthetics" and obligations around AI training licensing.

On digital replicas, an area of controversy that led the vast majority of Equity's member base to say they would refuse to be digitally scanned on-set, actors will now &#8220;have the right to be paid when your digital replica is used&#8221; and &#8220;have the right to consent to whether a digital replica of you is used and the right to information about the specific use prior to granting consent.&#8221;

Furthermore, a producer &#8220;cannot obtain blanket consent to your digital replica&#8221; but only for specific projects. Use of a digital replica or digital alteration will also &#8220;require an actor's approval if there are any substantive changes to scenes that are agreed as part of a nudity rider.&#8221;

Despite &#8220;our best efforts,&#8221; Equity noted it had failed to negotiate contractual protections for &#8220;digital replica deletion&#8221; or &#8220;digital scanning that is traditionally and/or customarily used in production for CGI, VFX and SFX and other digital technologies.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Equity's deal includes a 24% rise in pay rates for actors on movies budgeted over &#xA3;50M ($66M), which will take effect across the next three years (17% year 1), a 13% (7% year 1) uplift for movies budgeted between &#xA3;30M and &#xA3;50M, and a 9% increase on TV shows (3% per year).

In the thorny area of streamer compensation, which dominated the 2023 U.S. labor strikes, Equity has negotiated a 3 percentage point uplift to &#8220;streaming platform use fees,&#8221; effectively when a show is given a second window on a streamer. This could equate to a real term rise of as much as 50%, Equity said. The period during which these apply has been reduced from 15 years to 10, meaning actors will get secondary payments more quickly.

There are also &#8220;world-leading provisions&#8221; in another knotty area, casting self-tapes , with Equity including a 72-hour notice period for producers submitting scripts for self-tapes.

And coming amid the Russell Brand and David Walliams scandals, the deal introduces bullying and harassment principles commiting producers to safe casting and audition spaces, with training and reporting on sexual harassment and other workplace safety issues. For the first time ever, there are also sustainability provisions included in contracts, adopting a Green Rider to help improve the environmental impact of film and TV.

Equity's initial demands from way back in summer 2024 also centered on the end of special stipulations from the streamers. We understand these will likely be addressed in Equity's upcoming negotiations with the American SVoDs once the Pact deal is finalized.

Members are being asked to vote on the deal for the first time and are being recommended to say &#8220;yes.&#8221;

Equity General Secretary Paul W Fleming labeled the agreement &#8220;groundbreaking.&#8221;

&#8220;We set about to radically improve and modernise the terms and conditions for performers across UK TV and film,&#8221; he added. &#8220;The result is groundbreaking. We've achieved the best AI provisions in the business &#x2013; protecting performers and ensuring that human performance is valued and prioritised across the industry.&#8221;

The news comes after years of wrangling.

Unlike in the U.S., there is no cliff edge for these deals once previous contracts run down but they are instead constantly updated and tinkered with. So the stalemate has not led to what would have been an unprecedented strike, although it has certainly been discussed by Equity. Equity was a firm backer of SAG's cause during those headline-grabbing 2023 strikes.

Slow Horses will return for another two seasons.

The smash-hit Apple TV series is currently shooting its eighth installment in London, and speculation swiftly emerged that it could be the show's last &#x2014; especially with star player Jack Lowden in the running for James Bond and casting news on the next 007 imminent.

The streamer put those rumors to bed on Monday with the announcement of a ninth and tenth season, though only confirmed the return of Gary Oldman &#8216;s cantankerous leader of the spies, Jackson Lamb. Related Stories Movies Gerard Depardieu Drops Appeal Against Sexual Assault Conviction, Admits Guilt TV Nicola Coughlan "Will Not Be Watching" HBO's 'Harry Potter': "And I Would Never Be in It"

The espionage drama is adapted from Mick Herron's Slough House book series and currently co-stars Lowden as River Cartwright and Kristin Scott Thomas as Diana Taverner, as well as Saskia Reeves as Catherine Standish, Christopher Cho as tech expert Roddy, Rosalind Eleazar as Louisa, Aimee-Ffion Edwards as Shirley, Tom Brooke as JK Coe and Jonathan Pryce as David Cartwright. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The recently aired season six also saw the return of Hugo Weaving as Frank Harkness, River's birth father, and Olivia Cooke as Sid, an agent who was believed dead.

Asked if the show could continue if it were to outpace Herron's novels, executive producer Douglas Urbanski previously told THR : &#8220;Most TV shows don't have books, so we can figure this out. &#x2026; And there's another thing: Mick Herron hasn't stopped writing. I can't speak for Mick, but you never know, more books might be coming.&#8221;

Slow Horses is one of Apple TV's flagship shows. It's won three Emmy Awards, including two for outstanding directing for a drama series and one for outstanding writing for a drama series, and five BAFTA TV Awards, including writer, drama and two consecutive wins each for editing, fiction and sound. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The series is produced for Apple TV by See-Saw Films, with Jamie Laurenson, Hakan Kousetta, Douglas Urbanski, Iain Canning, Emile Sherman, Gail Mutrux, Billy Bowring, Mick Herron and Oldman serving as executive producers. See-Saw Films is part of the Mediawan group.

Nicola Coughlan won't be watching HBO's upcoming Harry Potter series.

The Bridgerton star sat down with British outlet The Observer to discuss her latest role in Channel 4's I Am Helen , the next installment of Dominic Savage's BAFTA-winning anthology series set to hit U.K. screens on Monday.

Published over the weekend, the interview sees the Derry Girls alum talk about her charity work and vocal support for Palestinian causes amid the ongoing Israel-Gaza war, including her raising over two million pounds ($2.6m) for Palestine while doing press for the Netflix Regency era behemoth. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Movies In 'The Matriarch,' Germany's First Film With an All-Vietnamese Lead Cast, Human Trafficking Thriller Meets Family Drama Movies Dystopian Thriller 'The Flaw' Is a Cinematic Puzzle About Totalitarianism: "Each One of Us Is a Regime"

She also, Rebecca Nicholson writes, marched for the legalization of abortion in her native Ireland and has consistently championed transgender rights. And last year, Coughlan was caught up in an online feud with Harry Potter author J.K. Rowling when the latter cheered on the U.K. Supreme Court's ruling on the legal definition of women, which declared it to be based on biological sex. Rowling responded to Coughlan at the time claiming that she did not know who Coughlan was, nor fellow critic Pedro Pascal.

&#8220;Me, I could believe," Coughlan told The Observer . "But Pedro Pascal? You know who Pedro Pascal is, girl. Like, please.&#8221;

Coughlan said she &#8220;loved&#8221; the Harry Potter books when she was younger. &#8220;But I will not be watching the new Harry Potter show and I would never be in it,&#8221; she added. &#8220;Look, I know people that are involved in those shows, and they're nice people and whatever, but it's not for me.&#8221;

Potter author Rowling, a staunch advocate for anti-trans policies in Britain, has regularly come under fire for her transphobia. She has often been publicly criticized over her politics and creation of The J.K. Rowling Women's Fund, a legal fund for individuals pushing anti-transgender views across the country. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The controversy has been renewed by the TV series, with stars John Lithgow (playing Albus Dumbledore), Nick Frost (Rubeus Hagrid) and Bel Powley (Petunia Dursley) among the castmembers distancing themselves from Rowling's views. She serves as an executive producer on the series, which hits HBO Max Dec. 25.

"I find it ironic and somewhat inexplicable that Rowling has expressed such views," said Lithgow earlier this year. "I've read about them, and I've never met her. She's not really involved in this production at all. The people who are readapting Harry Potter and turning it into an eight-year-long TV series are remarkable. &#x2026; These are people I really want to work with."

Coughlan said to The Observer that she credits her openness about her personal politics to seeing her parents &#8220;helping out, or being charitable, and not making a big deal of it.&#8221; With such a large social media following, she wanted to use that profile for the greater good. &#8220;In reality, people actually can help and make a difference. Six million followers is loads. But people have hundreds of millions. If you had 20 million, how much money could you raise?" she asked.

She admitted to feeling disappointed when other celebrities &#8220;with those bigger platforms&#8221; didn't &#8220;follow her into action.&#8221; Coughlan continues: &#8220;I had interesting conversations with certain people who said to me, &#x2018;I'm not in a strong enough position,' or &#x2018;I don't get to say anything, because my career is not as good', or &#x2018;I have too much to lose.' And I thought, this is bullshit, isn't it? Everyone has something to lose and everyone has something to gain. [&#8230;] I just think I would never forgive myself if I didn't say, &#x2018;I think this is really fucking wrong,' and I have a platform, and I want to try and do something practical, and that's to raise money.&#8221;
